* Roland TB-303 VCA, from the service notes (First Edition, 1982, p. 5; D275), with the envelope generator it shares
* its GATE, trigger and accent with (env.cir's circuit, repeated here so both run together): IC15 (BA662A) as its
* transistors, Q31 and Q32 setting its control current from C42, the accent's share through D27. The reference for
* CoolSynth 303's VCA. The audio inputs come from the filter's output (R121, C21) and the RESONANCE pot's wiper
* (R122, C22), as the x0xb0x's schematic (Open Music Labs' redraw) draws them; page 5 leaves them unlabelled.
*
* Parameters: as env.cir (decay, acc, accent, ton, toff, taoff), and amp, freq (the audio sine), res (RESONANCE's
* turn, 0..1), tend.
* The 12 V rail: IC16 makes it from the 5.333 V reference times 1 + R178 / R179 (2.2k / 1.8k), 11.85 V, not the 12 V
* drawn (D275); with 5 % resistors a unit may sit anywhere from about 11.4 to 12.3 V. vcc sets it.
.param decay=0.5 acc=0 accent=0.5 ton=10m toff=72.5m taoff=135m amp=0.3 freq=440 res=0.5 vcc=11.851 tend=0.5
.param ka=3.47
.param tdec={(exp(ka*decay)-1)/(exp(ka)-1)} rdec={max(1Meg*tdec, 1)}
.param racc1={max(50k*accent, 1)} racc3={max(50k*(1-accent), 1)}

.model QEM NPN(IS=39f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF=416.4 NE=1.259 ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m XTB=1.5 BR=.7371 NC=2
+ ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1 CJC=3.638p MJC=.3085 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=4.493p MJE=.2593 VJE=.75 TR=239.5n TF=301.2p ITF=.4
+ VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)
.model QPM PNP(IS=39f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=18.7 BF=300 NE=1.5 ISE=0 IKF=80m XTB=1.5 BR=4.977 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0
+ RC=2.5 CJC=9.728p MJC=.5776 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=8.063p MJE=.3677 VJE=.75 TR=33.42n TF=179.3p ITF=.4 VTF=4 XTF=6
+ RB=10)
.model JFY NJF(VTO=-1.5 BETA=0.89m LAMBDA=2m CGS=8p CGD=3p)
.model DEM D(IS=2.52n N=1.752 RS=0.568 CJO=2p)
.model SWI SW(VT=6 VH=0.5 RON=200 ROFF=1G)

VCC vcc 0 {vcc}
VR vr 0 5.333

* The gate, 0 or 5 V from the CPU.
VG ng 0 PWL(0 0 {ton} 0 {ton+1u} 5 {toff} 5 {toff+1u} 0)
R146 ng nb37 22k
R144 nb37 0 10k
Q37 nc37 nb37 0 QEM

* Q36: GATE.
R147 vcc ne36 22
R142 vcc nb36 10k
C72 vcc nb36 10u
R143 nb36 nc37 10k
Q36 ngate nb36 ne36 QPM
R145 ngate 0 10k

* Q38: the one-shot into C62.
R150 vcc ne38 22
C55 ne38 0 47u
R149 vcc nb38 10k
R148 nb38 n54 10k
C54 n54 nc37 0.047u
Q38 nc38 nb38 ne38 QPM
R151 nc38 0 22k
D37 nc38 n152 DEM
R152 n152 nc62 100
C62 nc62 0 1u

* The buffer: Q41 and Q40 over Q39 (gate and source to ground).
Q41 vcc nc62 ne41 QEM
Q40 vcc ne41 nenv QEM
J39 nenv 0 0 JFY

* The decay: R138 to the DECAY line, DECAY to the diode string; IC12B shorts DECAY on an accent.
VACC nacc 0 PWL(0 0 {ton} 0 {ton+1u} {acc} {taoff} {acc} {taoff+1u} 0)
R138 nc62 ndec 68k
RDEC ndec nn4 {rdec}
S12B ndec nn4 nacc 0 SWI
D28 nn4 nn3 DEM
D29 nn3 nn2 DEM
R117 vr nn2 22k
D26 nn2 0 DEM

* IC12A: the envelope to the ACCENT knob on an accent; its wiper toward the VCA (R119, C36) and the filter (D24).
S12A nenv nacc3 nacc 0 SWI
RACC3 nacc3 naccw {racc3}
RACC1 naccw 0 {racc1}
R119 naccw n36 47k
C36 n36 0 0.033u
R120 n36 n27 22k

* ENV MOD's load: 50k and R61 to the filter's VQ9.
RLOAD nenv nvq9 60k
VQ9 nvq9 0 3.31

* ---- The VCA ----

* The audio: the filter's output (C14's side) and the RESONANCE pot's wiper (res times it), here a sine of amp volts
* at freq Hz (the filter's output swings about +-0.3 V at TP6).
VAUD nvcf 0 SIN(0 {amp} {freq})
BRES nresw 0 V = {res} * v(nvcf)

* IC15's inputs: both at C37's 5.333 V (R126) through R125 and R124 (2.2k); the audio into pin 3 through R121 and C21
* (from the filter) and R122 and C22 (from the RESONANCE wiper).
R126 vr nm 2.2k
C37 nm 0 10u
R125 nm nin2 2.2k
R124 nm nin3 2.2k
C21 nvcf n21 0.01u
R121 n21 nin3 220k
C22 nresw n22 0.01u
R122 n22 nin3 100k

* The control current into pin 1: Q31 (2SA733) from GATE through D35, R133 and R131 (220k); its base on C42 (1 uF),
* which Q32 empties through R132 at each trigger (D36, R134, C41) and R123 (1.5 M) refills: the volume's own decay.
* The accent's share through R120 and D27. (D34 and R137 feed the GATE OUT jack from here; with nothing plugged in
* they carry nothing, so they are left out.)
D35 ngate n35 DEM
R133 n35 nx31 2.2k
R131 nx31 ne31 220k
Q31 niabc nb31 ne31 QPM
R123 vcc nb31 1.5Meg
C42 nb31 0 1u
R132 nb31 nc32 100
D36 nc38 n36d DEM
R134 n36d nb32 22k
C41 nb32 0 0.1u
Q32 nc32 nb32 ne32 QEM
R130 ne32 0 100
D27V n27 niabc DEM

* IC15, the BA662A: pin 9 and pin 4 to 12 V, pin 5 to ground.
XIC15 niabc nin2 nin3 vcc 0 nota nota nvout vcc BA662

* Its output's load: R128 (220k) and R127 (47k) side by side, R129 (22k) to C40's 5.333 V (R162 2.2k); the buffer
* (pins 7, 8) out through C38 to the mixer (taken as 100k).
R128 nota nn 220k
R127 nota nn 47k
R129 nn nq 22k
R162 vr nq 2.2k
C40 nq 0 10u
C38 nvout nout 1u
RMIX nout 0 100k

* The BA662 as Open Music Labs reverse-engineered it (openmusiclabs.com/wiki/x0xb0x, its BA662 page): Q1A and Q1B
* mirror pin 1's current (emitter resistors about 500 ohm, measured) to the pair Q2A (pin 2) and Q2B (pin 3); two PNP
* Wilson mirrors (Q3A, Q3B, Q5B; Q4A, Q4B, Q5A) and an NPN one (Q6A, Q6B, Q7B) make pin 6 the difference of the
* pair's currents; pin 7 to pin 8 a complementary follower (Q7A, Q10A, R21 11k), biased by Q9A mirroring Q9B's
* current from pin 4 through R20 (50k). Transistors: generic integrated NPN (hFE 150) and lateral PNP (hFE 50).
.subckt BA662 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9
Q1A p1 p1 e1a NI
R1A e1a p5 500
Q1B t p1 e1b NI
R1B e1b p5 500
Q2A ca p2 t NI
Q2B cb p3 t NI
Q3A ca b3 p9 PL
Q3B b3 b3 p9 PL
Q5B x ca b3 PL
Q4A cb b4 p9 PL
Q4B b4 b4 p9 PL
Q5A p6 cb b4 PL
Q6A x b6 p5 NI
Q6B b6 b6 p5 NI
Q7B p6 x b6 NI
R20 p4 b9 50k
Q9B b9 b9 p5 NI
Q9A e7 b9 p5 NI
Q7A p9 p7 e7 NI
Q10A p5 e7 p8 PL
R21 p9 p8 11k
.model NI NPN(IS=1f BF=150 VAF=100 CJE=1p CJC=0.5p TF=0.5n)
.model PL PNP(IS=1f BF=50 VAF=50 CJE=1p CJC=2p TF=20n)
.ends

.options method=trap reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-12 vntol=1e-7
.tran 10u {tend} 0 10u
.end
